            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Do you know what work is required for this? Happy to help if you're open to it.\r\n\r\nProbably some way of properly getting this offset information (in a backwards compatible down through Neovim 0.8 way; maybe have this only starting from some more recent version if the API is difficult) and apply it [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/9df78f3cdf9bdcc5aaf93cc51412a69a384041b2/lua/mini/ai.lua#L974-L978). I *think* this should be it, but can't vouch for that.\r\n\r\nIf you want to and have (lots of) free time, sure go ahead. But if not - no worries; I'll probably look at it this week.",
