        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Ah I understand now why the offset is ignored. The directive stores the adjusted range in the capture metadata, whereas mini.ai [only looks at the captured node](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/9df78f3cdf9bdcc5aaf93cc51412a69a384041b2/lua/mini/ai.lua#L1505).\r\n\r\nSee the relevant code in [nvim-treesitter-textobject](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects/blob/ad8f0a472148c3e0ae9851e26a722ee4e29b1595/lua/nvim-treesitter/textobjects/shared.lua#L192-L198).",
